General Guide to Creating a Seq2arch docker image


1. Gather various IDs from Seqera Cloud:

    a. Open the token tab on Seqera Cloud

    ![](image.png)

    b. Generate a new access token (or use an existing one if available). Make sure to have the access token locally


1. Gather relevant IDs from Seqera Cloud for GitHub Secrets
    a. Go to AWS Secrets Manager > Secrets > Store a new secret
    b. Choose secret type > Other type of secret
    c. For the following, enter in the key and your values:
        i.tower_access_token



__You should not need to edit the Dockerfile itself, but you may need to edit the following 5 files that get pulled in to the Dockerfile:__
1. profiles.py
2. clean_seqera.py
3. lambda_function.py
4. run_clean_seqera.sh
5. run_clean_seqera_dryrun.sh


